==Personality==
As shown in her dialogue and [[Introduction Card]], Brightney is a smart and helpful [[Toon]]. Like her Active [[Ability]] suggests, she is skilled at solving problems, as well as helping Toons out. However, she may likely be overworked at times.

Brightney seems to show her overworked side when she says, "{{Text|There's always something on my mind, {{CI|Boxten|name=true}}!}}" and "{{Text|Always have to be three steps ahead of those [[Twisteds]]!}}" which, when paired with the note in her [[Roleplay Mode|Roleplay room]] with a to-do list, and the messiness of said room, suggests a deeper side of being overworked. Despite this, she's always ready to help with whatever her fellow Toons ask of her, showing her personality as a hardworking and friendly Toon. She actively looks out for {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} and has a history of helping him with his work, open to any investigations. She seems to be sensitive when it comes to insults, which is shown in her interactions with both {{CI|Shelly|name=true}} and {{CI|Finn|name=true}}—in which she gets defensive and seemingly jumps to conclusions of people insulting her when her intellect is compared to other matters. Furthermore, in her and {{CI|Vee|name=true}}'s second interaction, it is shown that she craves validation and reassurance that she is intelligent when saying, "{{Text|Wait, like I'm truly talented as opposed to "un-truly" talented?|}}", showing a bit of possible self-doubt and ascertaining the fact that she is considered intelligent despite Vee's words being very clear. Fortunately, Rodger frequently compliments her in their interactions, making her feel more at peace with her own wit.

