==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.
*For the second requirement, go to multiple runs and avoid choose the {{CDI|Electrician|name=true}} card, since it reduces the chances of a [[Blackout]] occurring.

==Strategies==
Brightney is a great All-Rounded [[Toon]] who is best utilized by those familiar with the game. It's recommended to use her if you feel confident in your skills, as her biggest drawback, while potent, can be turned into a strength if used well. Her low [[Stealth]] can also be used to save Toons who have a harder time getting out of chases, such as {{CI|Soulvester|name=true}}, {{CI|Vee|name=true}}, {{CI|Rodger|name=true}}, and {{CI|Gigi|name=true}}.

Brightney works best during [[Blackouts]]. Her Active [[Ability]], {{AI|Brightney|name=true}}, is an incredibly useful Blackout-exclusive tool. It counters the primary threat of Blackouts, information loss, and helps teammates stay alive in the dangerous environment. Brightney's light during Blackouts is also notably brighter and larger than all other Toons, granting her high visibility and giving teammates a great source of light. Brightney is ultimately the best Toon for countering Blackouts survival-wise (though Vee comes extremely close), and can be crucial in helping the team. However, Vee may be a better option for the extraction side of things, since she can highlight both [[Twisteds]] and Machines, albeit for only three seconds shorter than Brightney can highlight. Vee's cooldown is also five seconds longer, but that really doesn't affect much.

Brightney's Blackout-countering Ability, high extraction, and above-average mobility makes her one of, if not '''the''' best Toon for solo runs, as her low Stealth becomes nearly (but not completely) a non-factor with the absence of other players dragging Twisteds to your location. It is recommended to use run speed [[Trinkets]] to boost survivability as her Extraction is already good. On later [[Floors]], knowing which Twisteds are present, and their locations is crucial for knowing how to tackle the Floor.

Not every Floor is a Blackout, but Brightney can still be useful outside them. She has a great [[Stat]] pool, with high Stamina and Extraction Speed at the cost of Stealth. To counteract her poor Stealth, Brightney can use her high Stamina to dash in and out of dangerous situations. Additionally, Brightney can temporarily help with diverting Twisteds using her high Stamina and low Stealth to help lure the Twisteds away from other Toons. With high skill, she can even be used to distract normal Twisteds indefinitely and can distract most Twisteds as well. It's also way easier to bring Twisteds to Distractors (namely {{CI|Pebble|name=true}}) since they'll lock onto you until you get out of their sight in most cases. However, you could get unneeded attention of dangerous Twisteds that are wandering around or being distracted, especially {{Type|Main}} Twisteds. The ones you should take most caution around are {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}}, {{CI|Twisted Coal|name=true}} (in a Blackout), {{CI|Twisted Bobette|name=true}}, and {{CI|Twisted Vee|name=true}} (situational due to {{TI|Train Whistle|name=true}} existing) since the prior three have almost the same speed as you, which will make them extremely hard to even outrun due to Brightney's 3 {{Star}} [[Movement Speed]], so having Items such as {{II|Speed Candy|name=true|plural=a}}, {{II|Protein Bar|name=false}}s, or {{II|Box o' Chocolates|name=false|plural=a}} can potentially help you escape. If you want to extract safely, check your surroundings and Distractor's location frequently to avoid getting cornered. Do note there also aren't any common Trinkets or Items that can aid Brightney's Stealth, due to it being 0 and all Stealth Trinkets and Items being percentage based, therefore providing no effect. The only Items that can help with Brightney's Stealth are {{II|Smoke Bomb|name=false}} and {{II|Eject Button|name=false}}, both of which are in the ultra rare tier and best saved for near-death situations, or to avoid using up Stamina. If there is a distractor, try to keep tabs on their location and stay away from them. If you do happen to be seen by the Twisteds, cut line of sight as fast as possible for the distractor to re-retrieve the Twisteds. However, her low Stealth can be used to help slower Toons struggling with fast Twisteds, or to help the distractor should they run out of Stamina. Speaking of Stamina, even though Brightney has a lot of it, you should manage it carefully. It's fine to sprint tap around the map to traverse faster, but don't waste all of it should your low Stealth get you in a chase.

Brightney can really help with completing [[Dyle's Floor]]. Her Stats allow her to extract all Machine types efficiently, though the low Stealth can endanger her if {{CI|Twisted Dyle|name=true}} becomes enraged, and other Toons without the same Stealth can easily lead Twisteds onto her. During Blackouts, she will be able to highlight where Twisted Dyle and the other Twisteds are, which can be extremely helpful as players can otherwise get caught off guard; her incredibly bright light radius can also make it a bit easier to navigate the Floor. The +50 Stamina gained from completing the Floor may not be so useful on paper since Brightney already has 175 Stamina, but her Stealth means she's more likely to get chased by Twisteds, which can especially be a problem on later Floors with more dangerous Twisteds. 

Brightney is one of the Toons with no best set of Items. She can mostly be used as a blank slate due to her above-average Stats. However, Stamina-restoring Items, such as Protein Bars and {{II|Stamina Candy|name=false|plural=a}}, are useful, as they'll help to maintain her above-average Stamina. Healing Items also tend to be useful, so it's good to keep them in your inventory if needed without clogging it. If you're not used to her abysmal Stealth, taking hits is near-guaranteed.

Overall, Brightney is pretty great at many things; whether it be extracting, gathering Twisteds, or protecting teammates. She's a great counter to Blackouts survival-wise, but also requires patience and communication if you wish to avoid taking Twisted aggro as much as possible.

