==Trivia==
*Brightney's name is a mixture of the feminine English name, "Britney" and the word, "bright". She fits both definitions of bright—as in literally emitting light from her lightbulb, and intellectually.
**Lightbulbs in cartoons also are often associated with ideas and intelligence.
*Similar to {{CI|Gigi|name=true}}, Brightney doesn't wear shoes, as the lighter color is actually the soles of her feet.
*Brightney's low [[Stealth]] most likely references to how her bright light gives her away to [[Twisteds]], similarly to her {{CI|Twisted Brightney}}[[Twisted Brightney|Twisted Counterpart]]'s light.
**Brightney's interactions with {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} and {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}, along with {{CI|Dandy|name=true}}'s [[Gossip]] about her reaffirm this.
*Brightney has stated she is in a book club, the other [[Toons]] in this Book Club are {{CI|Astro|name=true}} and {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle}}[[Dazzle]].
**Brightney is the president of said book club, as proven by her interaction with {{CI|Tisha|name=true}}.
**{{CI|Squirm|name=true}} used to be in the book club, but likely due to his bad habit of eating books, he was kicked out with no hard feelings.
*As revealed by {{CI|Bobette|name=true}}'s [[Gossip]], Brightney is able to direct the power within [[Gardenview]] despite the fact that it should logically be weaker after such a long time since the shutdown. The way she's able to do this is unknown.
**[[Dandy]]'s Gossip brings up Brightney doing unknown activities during late night hours. While the two pieces of Gossip may not be linked up, they both paint Brightney as a potentially suspicious character, or someone who knows something others don't.
*Brightney uses an incandescent light bulb, as shown in an interaction with {{CI|Flutter|name=true}}.
*{{CI|Twisted Rodger|name=true}} isn't highlighted when using Brightney's Active [[Ability]]. This remains true even when he is active.
*Brightney is {{CI|Vee|name=true}}'s favorite contestant, and the two seem to be on good terms.
**It is also implied that Brightney has back up batteries for Vee. In the Toon Rooms in [[Roleplay]] mode she has batteries on her nightstand, and in the "The Vee Virus" Episode [[Poster]], Brightney is seen carrying a box with the same batteries. This is also shown in the "Don't forget to recharge! 🔋" video, where she recharges Vee by putting batteries into her.
***With all of this as well as Brightney's general knowledge in technology and electricity, it's established that she takes care of Vee.
**Vee needing Brightney's completed [[Mastery]] could reaffirm their friendship.
***This could also reflect their Active [[Abilities]] similarities, both highlighting [[Twisteds]], them being Light-Producing [[Toons]], and their Statistic similarities (high extractability with low Stealth).
*As seen in an interaction with {{CI|Poppy|name=true}}, Brightney considers her lampshade to be red, not pink.
*According to her dialogue with {{CI|Pebble|name=true}}, Brightney seems to pertain an interest in geology.
*If you look inside her hollow head, Brightney's lampshade is not connected to her lightbulb in any way.
*According to Brightney, if she really wanted to, she can change the color in which her lightbulb emits as shown in an interaction with {{CI|Rudie|name=true}}, meaning it isn't a vital part of her body.
*Brightney's eyes glow in the dark, as seen in the TV animation for [[Vee's Floor]].
*Before [[Changelog|v0.4]], {{TI|Diary|name=true}} could have actually worked on Brightney, as it used to add 2.5 units to her Stealth [[Stat]] instead of a 25% multiplier.
**Now, the [[Trinket]] does not affect her Stealth and remains at 0 units.
*Brightney, [[Pebble]], and [[Razzle & Dazzle]] (because of '''Comedy/Tragedy'''), are one of the first [[Toons]] to have 1{{Star}} on a Statistic and to not be [[Shrimpo]].
*Brightney likely wears glasses, as seen in an official doodle and in her {{Skin|Antique Shade}} and {{Skin|Cozy Lighting}} [[Skins]].
**Since she doesn't always seem to wear them, it's possible they're specifically reading glasses, as opposed to a pair she needs to wear constantly.
*Despite Brightney looking like she has a neck, it is actually the rod that holds her light bulb up.
*Brightney, {{CI|Goob|name=true}}, and {{CI|Scraps|name=true}} are the last [[Toons]] to get optimized. She is also the last {{Type|Uncommon}} Toon to be optimized.
*Brightney's {{Skin|Cozy Lighting}} and {{Skin|Batty Shade}} [[Skins]] are currently her only ones that glow a color other than white in [[Blackouts]].
*Brightney was the only non-{{Type|Main}} [[Toon]] to be Light-Producing, until {{CI|Connie|name=true}} was added.
*Despite Brightney's to-do list in her [[Roleplay|Roleplay room]] including a task written as "Help {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} organize", her room is very messy, with trash (such as crumpled paper) and books cluttered around. This could be the reason Rodger requests for {{CI|Tisha|name=true}}'s assistance with organizing, despite a deeper level of trust between him and Brightney, even stating "{{Text|Yes, well, some of my trusted friends don't know how to organize well.|}}".

